{"id": "parks-alliance-accounts-to-collapse", "title": "Parks Alliance: from a director's off-book account to a missing-money collapse", "seconds": 137.5, "voice": "elevenlabs:9PVP7ENhDskL0KYHAKtD", "narrator": "Jerry B.", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "e0ac2cef37de7b72", "words": 426, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "The San Francisco Parks Alliance was the City’s main parks charity.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 3.24, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "San Francisco Parks Alliance", "sub": "the City’s main “friends of” charity for parks"}, "wt": [0.03, 0.09, 0.29, 0.82, 1.08, 1.49, 1.66, 1.75, 2.08, 2.3, 2.62]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "It also held accounts for Public Works.", "t0": 3.36, "t1": 5.03, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "San Francisco Parks Alliance", "sub": "the City’s main “friends of” charity for parks"}, "emph": ["Public Works"], "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.32, 0.46, 0.79, 0.94, 1.28]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[2]"], "text": "Public Works director Mohammed Nuru ran them.", "t0": 5.15, "t1": 7.32, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "City contractors", "sub": "asked to donate"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Public Works accounts", "sub": "held at the Parks Alliance"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Mohammed Nuru", "sub": "Public Works director, directed the spending"}], "kicker": "Off the City’s books"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.48, 0.82, 1.24, 1.64, 1.88]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[2]"], "text": "He asked companies with City contracts to give. None of it touched the City’s books.", "t0": 7.44, "t1": 11.07, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "City contractors", "sub": "asked to donate"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Public Works accounts", "sub": "held at the Parks Alliance"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Mohammed Nuru", "sub": "Public Works director, directed the spending"}], "kicker": "Off the City’s books"}, "emph": ["none of it"], "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.29, 0.68, 0.82, 1.03, 1.47, 1.58, 2.06, 2.34, 2.45, 2.54, 2.85, 2.94, 3.22]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "established[0]"], "text": "After Nuru’s arrest, the Controller added it up. How much went in?", "t0": 11.19, "t1": 15.19, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "The Public Works accounts", "sub": "July 2015 to January 17, 2020"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.63, 1.26, 1.35, 1.83, 2.15, 2.31, 2.71, 3.15, 3.33, 3.51]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "992,830 dollars.", "t0": 15.19, "t1": 18.19, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$992,830", "label": "into the Public Works accounts", "sub": "$966,247 from City contractors and permit holders"}, "emph": ["992,830"], "wt": [0.04, 0.34, 0.64, 1.17, 1.74, 1.93, 2.15, 2.49]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["sources"], "text": "That’s an official finding, by the City Controller, in 2020.", "t0": 18.71, "t1": 21.58, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "An official finding", "sub": "San Francisco Controller’s Office, September 24, 2020"}, "emph": ["official finding"], "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.25, 0.59, 1.17, 1.23, 1.32, 1.52, 2.13, 2.24, 2.45]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["established[1]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "721,250 dollars came through another charity, the Clean City Coalition.", "t0": 21.8, "t1": 27.24, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "van", "name": "Recology", "sub": "the garbage company"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "SF Clean City Coalition", "sub": "passed it on"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Public Works accounts", "sub": "$721,250"}], "kicker": "The biggest donor"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.51, 1.0, 1.57, 1.7, 1.99, 2.31, 2.65, 2.89, 3.1, 3.38, 4.02, 4.13, 4.52, 4.79]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["established[1]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "It was passing on money from Recology, the garbage company.", "t0": 27.36, "t1": 29.99, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "van", "name": "Recology", "sub": "the garbage company"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "SF Clean City Coalition", "sub": "passed it on"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Public Works accounts", "sub": "$721,250"}], "kicker": "The biggest donor"}, "emph": ["Recology"], "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.24, 0.58, 0.7, 0.91, 1.12, 1.75, 1.84, 2.18]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[3]"], "text": "Money went out to firms tied to insiders.", "t0": 30.11, "t1": 31.96, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Paid out of the accounts (five vendors got almost $370,000)", "rows": [["SDL Merchandising", "164,885"], ["Walter Wong’s companies", "41,673"], ["Lefty O’Doul’s businesses", "25,327"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.32, 0.46, 0.61, 0.92, 1.13, 1.27]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[3]"], "text": "164,885 dollars to SDL Merchandising, owned by a then Public Works employee.", "t0": 32.08, "t1": 38.26, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Paid out of the accounts (five vendors got almost $370,000)", "rows": [["SDL Merchandising", "164,885"], ["Walter Wong’s companies", "41,673"], ["Lefty O’Doul’s businesses", "25,327"]]}, "emph": ["164,885"], "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.39, 0.92, 1.43, 1.63, 1.9, 2.38, 2.82, 3.1, 3.44, 4.34, 4.58, 4.73, 4.84, 5.05, 5.38, 5.64]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[4]", "defense[0]", "notEstablished[4]"], "text": "The Alliance said it didn’t know, and didn’t profit.", "t0": 38.38, "t1": 40.49, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "it did not know its fiscal agency was being used unscrupulously"}, "emph": ["didn’t know"], "wt": [0.0, 0.03, 0.54, 0.72, 0.81, 1.13, 1.4, 1.53, 1.75]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "The partnership went on. In 2021, the Board’s analyst found its controls against corruption lacking.", "t0": 40.71, "t1": 46.22, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Controls against corruption lacking", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst, 2021"}, "emph": ["lacking"], "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.58, 0.83, 1.4, 1.63, 1.84, 2.62, 2.71, 3.04, 3.38, 3.64, 3.78, 4.18, 4.51, 4.99]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "suspicious[1].what", "established[5]", "established[22]", "established[23]"], "text": "City departments kept paying the Alliance about 3 million dollars a year, through 2024.", "t0": 46.34, "t1": 51.09, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["City payments to the Alliance, FY2019", "$3.24M"], "b": ["FY2024", "$2.86M"], "arrows": false, "mid": "largest line: $4,472,507 from Economic and Workforce Development, for 31 public spaces"}, "emph": ["kept paying"], "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.72, 0.97, 1.22, 1.32, 1.77, 1.98, 2.25, 2.64, 3.0, 3.12, 3.48, 3.64, 3.9]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[3]", "suspicious[2]"], "text": "In spring 2025, park groups couldn’t get their money out.", "t0": 51.31, "t1": 54.56, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Restricted gifts", "kicker": "Spring 2025, as KQED reported", "sub": "given for specific projects, spent on running costs", "chip": "at least $3.8 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.42, 0.66, 1.48, 1.69, 2.01, 2.28, 2.4, 2.54, 2.78]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[3]", "suspicious[2]"], "text": "KQED reported the board chair acknowledged at least 3.8 million dollars of project gifts paid running costs.", "t0": 54.68, "t1": 59.95, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Restricted gifts", "kicker": "Spring 2025, as KQED reported", "sub": "given for specific projects, spent on running costs", "chip": "at least $3.8 million"}, "emph": ["3.8 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.58, 0.9, 0.99, 1.26, 1.51, 1.92, 2.05, 2.25, 2.47, 2.76, 2.85, 3.19, 3.5, 3.6, 3.99, 4.27, 4.51, 4.8]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "story[3]"], "text": "Mission Local reported at least 5.4 million dollars owed to community groups.", "t0": 60.07, "t1": 64.27, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$5.4 million", "label": "at least, owed to community groups", "sub": "as Mission Local reported"}, "emph": ["Owed"], "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.65, 1.05, 1.17, 1.39, 1.67, 2.03, 2.19, 2.65, 3.06, 3.31, 3.44, 3.78]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "span", "ref": ["established[13]", "story[3]"], "text": "The Mayor froze City funding on May 23, 2025. On June 3, the Alliance shut down.", "t0": 64.79, "t1": 70.59, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2025-05-23", "to": "2025-06-03", "days": null, "fromLab": "Mayor freezes City funding", "toLab": "Alliance shuts down", "kicker": "The end"}, "emph": ["shut down"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.4, 0.79, 1.04, 1.38, 1.52, 1.7, 2.36, 2.57, 3.69, 3.79, 4.06, 4.55, 4.64, 5.04, 5.27]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[17]"], "text": "Its own 2024 renewal report admitted negative net assets, and a large unsecured loan it was renegotiating.", "t0": 70.71, "t1": 76.69, "shot": "b12a", "visual": {"type": "quote", "kicker": "Its 2024 renewal report", "line": "shows negative net assets"}, "emph": ["negative net assets"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.34, 0.6, 1.02, 1.42, 1.74, 2.08, 2.49, 2.7, 3.4, 3.6, 3.69, 4.04, 4.56, 4.79, 4.87, 5.02]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[19]"], "text": "In July 2024 its chief executive swore all restricted funds were used for their purposes.", "t0": 76.81, "t1": 81.87, "shot": "b12b", "visual": {"type": "quote", "kicker": "Report to the Attorney General, signed 25 July 2024", "line": "all restricted funds were used in a manner consistent with their respective restricted purposes"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.34, 0.6, 1.19, 1.48, 1.75, 2.24, 2.62, 2.82, 3.36, 3.68, 3.89, 4.14, 4.26, 4.43]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["notEstablished[6]"], "text": "Whether that was false when signed isn’t shown: it covered the year to June 2023.", "t0": 81.99, "t1": 86.24, "shot": "b12b", "visual": {"type": "quote", "kicker": "Report to the Attorney General, signed 25 July 2024", "line": "all restricted funds were used in a manner consistent with their respective restricted purposes"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.35, 0.56, 0.86, 1.02, 1.34, 1.56, 2.22, 2.34, 2.59, 2.68, 2.88, 3.02, 3.27, 3.48]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[4]", "established[10]"], "text": "In 2026, a Controller audit sampled 1,700,038 dollars", "t0": 86.46, "t1": 90.29, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Controller audit, June 9, 2026", "kicker": "The second official finding", "sub": "89 payments sampled, $1,700,038"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.29, 1.08, 1.15, 1.56, 1.83, 2.17, 2.48, 2.64, 2.95, 3.16, 3.5]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[4]", "established[10]"], "text": "of the Alliance’s payments for Rec and Park.", "t0": 90.29, "t1": 92.32, "shot": "b13x", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Controller audit, June 9, 2026", "kicker": "The second official finding", "sub": "89 payments sampled, $1,700,038"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.12, 0.26, 0.73, 1.1, 1.22, 1.43, 1.55]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[4]", "established[10]"], "text": "How much lacked proper records?", "t0": 92.44, "t1": 94.16, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Controller audit, June 9, 2026", "kicker": "The second official finding", "sub": "89 payments sampled, $1,700,038"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.41, 0.69, 1.02]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[9]"], "text": "848,670 dollars. Half.", "t0": 94.16, "t1": 98.26, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$848,670", "label": "without adequate documentation", "sub": "$838,507 of it from the India Basin Park fund"}, "emph": ["848,670"], "wt": [0.04, 0.34, 0.57, 1.04, 1.53, 1.81, 2.03, 2.44, 3.45]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[10]", "established[11]", "established[12]"], "text": "Nearly all from one fund, India Basin Park. And it had no written conflict-of-interest process.", "t0": 98.78, "t1": 103.95, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "no written conflict-of-interest process; the fiscal 2023 audited report still unfinished in October 2024"}, "emph": ["India Basin"], "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.46, 0.67, 0.9, 1.54, 1.87, 2.23, 2.73, 2.89, 2.98, 3.2, 3.37, 3.72, 4.6]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].what", "suspicious[3].why"], "text": "In October 2024, the Alliance gave a ballot campaign", "t0": 104.17, "t1": 107.21, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Healthy, Vibrant SF, Yes on B", "kicker": "October 2024", "sub": "a ballot-measure committee", "chip": "$76,337.65"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.47, 0.74, 1.52, 1.61, 2.01, 2.2, 2.27, 2.56]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].what", "suspicious[3].why"], "text": "76,337.65 dollars.", "t0": 107.21, "t1": 110.75, "shot": "b17x", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Healthy, Vibrant SF, Yes on B", "kicker": "October 2024", "sub": "a ballot-measure committee", "chip": "$76,337.65"}, "emph": ["76,337.65"], "wt": [0.04, 0.71, 1.15, 1.28, 1.5, 1.97, 2.37, 2.56, 3.06]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].what", "suspicious[3].why"], "text": "Former leaders said, Mission Local reported, they knew of a shortage four months earlier.", "t0": 110.87, "t1": 115.21, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Healthy, Vibrant SF, Yes on B", "kicker": "October 2024", "sub": "a ballot-measure committee", "chip": "$76,337.65"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.59, 1.1, 1.39, 1.71, 2.56, 2.71, 2.89, 2.97, 3.05, 3.51, 3.7, 3.91]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "suspicious[4].what", "suspicious[4].why"], "text": "Rec and Park’s chief, Phil Ginsburg, reported two 2019 trips it paid for. He oversaw its agreements.", "t0": 115.33, "t1": 120.94, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Long Island NY, May 2019", "$911.61"], "b": ["Seattle, September 2019", "$622.29"], "arrows": false, "mid": "trips paid by the Alliance"}, "emph": ["Phil Ginsburg"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.24, 0.57, 0.9, 1.11, 1.71, 2.17, 2.37, 2.55, 2.84, 3.25, 3.55, 3.64, 3.91, 4.48, 4.58, 4.96, 5.1]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "The records don’t show money stolen, rather than spent on running costs.", "t0": 121.16, "t1": 124.37, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That money was stolen, not spent on running costs", "Whether the ballot money came from restricted funds"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.37, 0.63, 0.77, 0.99, 1.57, 1.83, 1.98, 2.24, 2.38, 2.73]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? The promised public-integrity report, and the District Attorney’s decision.", "t0": 124.49, "t1": 128.82, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The joint City Attorney and Controller public-integrity report"}, {"who": "", "what": "The District Attorney’s charging decision"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.27, 0.54, 0.82, 0.96, 1.42, 2.23, 2.86, 2.92, 3.01, 3.35, 3.82]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "established[16]"], "text": "No one has been charged. On October 7, 2026, that review was still under way.", "t0": 128.94, "t1": 134.57, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.34, 0.45, 0.57, 1.37, 2.09, 2.48, 2.87, 3.07, 3.8, 3.96, 4.27, 4.42, 4.67, 4.91]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 134.69, "t1": 136.64, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.59, 0.71, 0.9, 0.97, 1.07, 1.32, 1.54]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The finding", "lead1": "Contractor money", "lead2": "$3 million a year", "lead3": "The collapse", "lead4": "Half undocumented", "lead5": "A campaign and two trips", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "kinetic", "hook": "document"}